# Jazz Comping: Drop-2 Voicings (repertoire plan: st-jazz-drop2). An original 16-bar comping
# study on the ii-V-I, in four-note drop-2 voicings on the top four strings.
# In C: Dm7 (xx3535: F C D A), G7 (xx3433: F B D G), Cmaj7 (xx2413: E B C G). Each voice moves
# as little as it can. Dm7 to G7: F stays, C goes down to B, D stays, A goes down to G.
# G7 to Cmaj7: F goes down to E, B stays, D goes down to C, G stays. Two notes move by a step at
# each change, two stay where they are.
# In F (from bar 9): the same three shapes moved up 5 frets: Gm7 (x-x-8-10-8-10),
# C7 (x-x-8-9-8-8), Fmaj7 (x-x-7-9-6-8), with exactly the same voice leading.
# Rhythm: half notes first, so you can hear each voice move; then the Charleston (a chord on
# beat 1 and a push on the swung "and" of 2, held through beats 3 and 4). Swing: the "and" is
# the last third of the beat, written as a triplet quarter rest (q3) then a triplet eighth (e3).
# The teacher walks a bass line in quarter notes.
title: Jazz Comping: Drop-2 Voicings
